  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "During Apollo 11, the 1969 mission that first landed people on the Moon, the crew is said to have been watched by craft on the lunar surface and followed on the way there, with the astronaut Neil Armstrong speaking on a private channel after landing. The scientist Steve Colbern, who studies objects said to be alien implants, repeats this from unnamed whistleblowers at NASA, the US space agency, who he says reported that Armstrong \"was on a private channel after landing on the moon.\" If true, it would mean the first Moon landing had company that was kept off the public broadcast."
